{"ld": 1619, "paper": "HP1073", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, to Direct the Governor's Energy Office to Solicit Information Regarding the Creation of a Thermal Energy Networks Program in Maine (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "h-runte-walter", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-mcintyre-mathew"], "committee_code": "EUT", "committee_name": "Energy, Utilities and Technology", "summary": {"text": "This resolve establishes the Commission to Study Pathways for Creating a Thermal Energy Networks Program in Maine. The commission is composed of legislators and public members, including, but not limited to, members with experience in engineering, research in the fields of thermal energy network development and workforce development. The resolve requires the commission to study the feasibility of implementing thermal energy networks for residential, commercial and industrial sectors in this State by examining a number of considerations, including, but not limited to, compatibility with existing systems, certain legal considerations, grid impacts, labor and workforce considerations and funding opportunities.\n\nThe commission must submit a report of its findings and recommendations to the Joint Standing Committee on Energy, Utilities and Technology by December 3, 2025. The committee may report out legislation related to the report to the Second Regular Session of the 132nd Legislature.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1073&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed", "date": "2025-06-11", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-06-11"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1619)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1073&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (H-411)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?pape